  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226505/assets/4745f9e651eb50c345550e83ee82eb957cd28fd82e3398b667e4285bb512194c.png)\n\nSolve for $x$ in the figure above given that $\\overset{⟷}{AB}∥\\overset{⟷}{CD}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the angles $∠JID$ and $∠EJB$ are corresponding angles, they are congruent and therefore have the same measure:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠JID & =m∠EJB \\\\ 4x+{25}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘}-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have an equation that we can solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+{25}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘}-x \\\\ 5x+{25}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 5x & ={155}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & =\\frac{{155}^{∘}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{5}x}{\\cancel{5}} & ={31}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={31}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
